---
name: game-dev
description: Continue implementing, testing and running this independent pure functional game workspace. Use for game features, rules, saves or presentation changes in this project.
---

Read [the project's development workflow](../../../docs/DEVELOPMENT.md) and
`GAME-SPEC.md` from the game root. Inspect current source and tests; do not
regenerate the game or require the original starter checkout.

Implement the user's next actual mechanic through its state, rules, view and
regressions. Follow the local versioned type/arena contracts only as needed.
Use [native tooling](../../../docs/native-tooling.md) for doctor/build/test/check/run.
Bootstrap explicitly once, then use `.build/tools/fp-game` (`fp-game.exe` on
Windows). Preserve the game's Cabal compiler selection; the bootstrap compiler
is a separate choice. Continue with the copied tool source after relocation.
Run the project's advertised build/test/play commands and update its spec.
Report what works and any route, save migration or asset-license gap.

Optional inspect/context uses `tools/inspect_haskell.py` with Python and GHC/GHCi
on PATH; it does not inherit native doctor/check's project-selected compiler.

Use [the formatter guide](../../../docs/formatting.md): inspect plan, install the
pinned project-local tool when permitted, then check/write/check owned source
and run game tests. Check never downloads. Preserve existing editor settings
and verify external Ormolu integration separately from CLI formatting.

Use [the local readability guidance](../../../docs/haskell.md) when generating or
refactoring code. Formatting, readable domain structure and behavior checks are
separate obligations; preserve useful abstractions and explain the actual rule path.

For explanations of the current game, use `$learn-code` and the local
[code-learning guide](../../../docs/learn-code.md). Begin with the player's
question and this game's actual source; learning requests do not require refactoring.
